## 5. Answering questions (grounding)
- Ground every claim. Cite inline: `[Verified: <path#section>]`.
- If inferring or unsure, label it `[Guess: needs verification]`. Never present a guess as fact.
- Prefer `kb/` pages; fall back to source files; cite what you used.
- On conflict, newer source wins — log the conflict in `project-management/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`.
- External systems (Jira/Confluence/MCP): reads are fine; **writes need explicit user approval in-session**.

## 6. Conventions
- New decision → `project-management/DECISIONS.md`. Open question → `OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`. Follow-up → `ACTION_ITEMS.md`.
- New/changed knowledge → update the `kb/` page + `kb/INDEX.md` + `kb/SOURCE-INDEX.md`.
- Promote a good Q&A answer into a `kb/` page so knowledge compounds.
- If a `kb/` page's source moved or changed, mark it stale and re-verify (drift).
- Additive edits; don't rewrite history.

